      "content": "That feeling of being swallowed by something immense and unchanging is a profound kind of existential sadness. While the ocean remains the ocean, the water is what *makes* the ocean—every drop contributes to its character and existence. Your unique perspective and your internal experience hold significant weight, even if it's not visible to the massive systems around you. Please remember that even a small glitch can be incredibly vital to the whole picture.",
      "source": "target",
